 "overview": "The Medford Bicycle Advisory Commission advises the city on bicycle infrastructure, cycling safety, and community outreach. The archive covers eighteen meetings held between March 2023 and September 2026. Over this span, the commission has focused on expanding municipal bike lanes, deploying safety equipment, consulting on regional paths, and coordinating with city departments and police. In its most recent meeting in September 2026, the commission reviewed strategic goals, approved a bulk purchase of bicycle lights, addressed board vacancies, and prepared advocacy priorities for discussions with the interim police chief.",
