  {
   "name": "Safety equipment and gear distribution",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission manages regular distributions of bike lights and safety helmets for local schools and public events, supported by bank sponsorships and donations (M01#2, M01#7). When its initial free helmet distribution program through Project KidSafe ceased, the commission formed a working group to investigate municipal procurement rules, alternative funding, and corporate sponsors (M12#8, M13#7, M14#6). By mid-2026, the commission sought city budget support for youth helmets (M15#7). In September 2026, the commission authorized spending $1,100 to purchase 960 bike lights offset by a recurring sponsorship, while allocating lights to student clubs (M18#3, M18#7).",
