  {
   "name": "Police engagement and road safety advocacy",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "In September 2024, the commission voted to establish a working group to coordinate with the mayor and police department on responses to aggressive driving and driver harassment following a road rage incident (M09#4, M10#2). The working group sought dedicated bicycle patrols, officer safety training, and the addition of a harassment category to the city's SeeClickFix platform (M12#6, M13#4). Following a cyclist fatality in mid-2026, the commission formed another working group to engage police on safety enforcement, incident tracking, and dooring collision reporting (M16#9, M17#2). In September 2026, the body outlined formal advocacy priorities to bring to an upcoming meeting with the interim police chief (M18#11).",
