  {
   "name": "State roadway safety and rotary redesigns",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The commission frequently advocates for safety upgrades on state corridors controlled by the Department of Conservation and Recreation and MassDOT (M03#3, M03#6, M08#4). In late 2024, members voted to endorse lowering speed limits to 25 miles per hour on state-owned roads in Medford and supported requests for state safety improvements (M10#4, M10#6, M11#5). Following an unannounced repainting of the Route 60 rotary in 2025 that the commission deemed substandard, the board sent a protest letter to DCR and partnered with Arlington's advisory committee on joint safety marking proposals (M13#9, M14#2). The commission continues to monitor state projects, including MassDOT path underpasses and Mystic River bridge contracts, while seeking improved coordination during state design phases (M17#4, M18#2).",
